<title>USA: WinStar completes $115 mln acquisition.</title>
<headline>WinStar completes $115 mln acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>WinStar Communications Inc said Friday it had completed the acquisition of Milliwave LP for about $115 million in cash and stock.</p>
<p>WinStar said it paid $40 million in cash and 3.6 million shares of stock worth about $75 million.</p>
<p>It said the acquisition significantly expands its wireless coverage, adding a new channel in 36 existing WinStar markets and adding more than 50 new major markets to its operating territories.</p>
<p>Dennis Patrick, Milliwave chief executive since June 1996, has joined WinStar's board. Patrick was chairman of the Federal Communications Commission from 1987 to 1989.</p>
